        "subject": "LU-20076 tests: keep sanity-hsm grace_delay over restarts",
        "message": "LU-20076 tests: keep sanity-hsm grace_delay over restarts\n\nsanity-hsm sets hsm.grace_delay to 10 without -P, so the MDT\nrestart in 26e puts back the default of 60, and 37, 40 and 90\nthen wait 61 s each in wait_for_grace_delay.  Set it with -P\nas well, and delete that at the end of the suite.\n\ncdt_set_mount_state() slept 20 s after its set_param -P.  Poll\nuntil hsm_control shows the new state instead, and keep the\nsleep only when the state asked for is already the current one,\nsince the late apply cannot be seen then.\n\nOn a four node cluster sanity-hsm takes 1621 s instead of\n1840 s: 37, 40 and 90 save about 50 s each, 26e, 300 and 409b\n18 to 35 s.  That is about 350 h per 30 days of CI.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-hsm,sanity-pcc\nTest-Parameters: trivial mdscount=2 mdtcount=4 testlist=sanity-hsm\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Id7f568eb37c14df3e74d2c748283c44f7603c860\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70383\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
